class.description:
The set variable node has the flow input [code]in[/code], the data input [code]value[/code] (any type) and the flow output [code]out[/code]. When the execution reaches it, the value of [code]value[/code] is stored in the variable [member FlowVariableNode.variable_name] of the blackboard and the execution continues at [code]out[/code].
At runtime the node reads [code]value[/code] when it is entered, writes it to the variable [member FlowVariableNode.variable_name] of the blackboard of the [FlowGraphPlayback] (which emits [signal FlowGraphPlayback.variable_changed]) and continues at [code]out[/code].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var set_gold := FlowSetVariableNode.new()
set_gold.variable_name = &"gold"
var set_id := graph.add_node(set_gold)
graph.connect_nodes(expression_id, "result", set_id, "value")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var setGold = new FlowSetVariableNode { VariableName = "gold" };
int setId = graph.AddNode(setGold);
graph.ConnectNodes(expressionId, "result", setId, "value");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
